<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - July 5.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - July 5.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended July 5</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     355	   1.51     697900  247.75   22.18</p>
<p>Telco		  440	   1.85     260150  114.47   21.92</p>
<p>TISCO		  220	   0.74     417400   91.83   17.54</p>
<p>ITC (BC)	     535	  29.74     130800   69.98   72.46</p>
<p>Castrol		535	   2.43     123350   65.99   23.68</p>
<p>ACC		   1510	   5.59	27550   41.60   19.30</p>
<p>BSES (BC)	    230	  13.50     174550   40.15   76.51</p>
<p>BHEL		   400	   1.82	78100   31.24   23.73</p>
<p>Oriental Bank	 69	   0.29     431300   29.76   21.92</p>
<p>STERLITE	     265	   1.06     108800   28.83   20.86</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 27.29 percent on an annualised basis against 29.37 percent in the previous carry forward account ended June 28.</p>
<p>Note :- BC - Book Closure</p>
